Let the app override the platform's gesture tuning, and tune the fling ceiling.

What: `App::set_gesture_tuning(GestureTuning)` stores an override; `App::gesture_tuning()` returns it, else the
platform's `PlatformGestures::tuning()`, else `GestureTuning::default()`. `Window::new` reads `cx.gesture_tuning()`
once, builds its touch recognizer from it (before: the platform's tuning only) and passes it to the backend in the
new `WindowParams::gesture_tuning`, so a window keeps the tuning it opened with. gpui_web's tap-candidate shadow in
`events.rs`, which mirrors the recognizer's slop to decide synchronously whether a touch release may open the
keyboard, reads that window's slop (`WebWindowInner::touch_slop`) instead of `GestureTuning::default()`, so it agrees
with the recognizer under any tuning. `GestureTuning` gains `max_fling_velocity` (default `ScrollPhysics::ios()`'s,
kMaxFlingVelocity), which the recognizer clamps a release to in place of the constant. Adds a window test with one
row per override (none, 18 px, 4 px) checking that a touch of a given travel taps or pans, and a recognizer test
that a flick flings at the tuned ceiling (8000 and 64000 px/s).

Why: the recognizer's slops, timeouts and fling physics come only from `Platform::gestures()`, which each upstream
backend fills with its own values (GPUI's defaults, Flutter's constants since 0013; the web's user-agent physics).
Parallax ports Flutter's per-platform values (Android's 8 dp device touch slop, `ClampingScrollPhysics` and the
least-squares tracker on Android, Linux and Windows, macOS's fast deceleration with its 8x fling ceiling) into one
visible target -> behaviour table in parallax-platform and lets apps override it (AGENTS.md "Platform feel"). Without
this patch that table could reach the recognizer only by patching every backend's `gestures()` (splitting the table
across crates) or by wrapping the whole `Platform` trait. The fling ceiling was a constant, so macOS's
`BouncingScrollPhysics(decelerationRate: fast)` ceiling could not reach the recognizer. The web's shadow had to
follow, or a touch travelling between the default slop and a smaller tuned one would tap (and focus a field) without
opening the keyboard. No cfg: the override is core and the same on every platform.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

